<O2Layout title="Privacy & community"><section class="wrap text-page"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY & COMMUNITY</span><h1>Your information.<br/><em>Handled thoughtfully.</em></h1><p>Last updated October 12, 2026. This page explains what this O2 Media website collects and how its features use that information.</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>Reader accounts</h2><p>Account creation uses Netlify Identity to manage your email address, display name, password credentials, confirmation emails, and authentication sessions. Your display name appears next to comments you submit. Do not put sensitive personal information in your display name or comments.</p><h2>Saved stories and comments</h2><p>Saved stories are associated with your account identifier and are visible through your reader account. Comments are stored with your account identifier, display name, text, and submission date. Approved comments are public. Pending and rejected comments remain accessible to the editorial team.</p><h2>Newsletter interest</h2><p>When you opt in, we store your email address and the date of your consent. The sign-up confirmation provides a private unsubscribe link for new subscriptions; save that link if you would like to remove your subscription later. You can also request removal through the contact form.</p><p>This website collects newsletter signups but does not automatically send marketing campaigns. Administrators can export the subscriber list for their email workflow. Any future newsletter should identify its sender and include a working unsubscribe option.</p><h2>Contact messages</h2><p>The contact form stores your name, email, subject, message, and submission date in the editorial inbox. Administrators can read, reply using their email application, and delete messages. Submitting a contact message does not subscribe you to marketing updates.</p><h2>Website services</h2><p>Netlify hosts this website, provides authentication, and stores application records in Netlify Database. Google Fonts is used for typography, which involves a request from your browser to Google. Article images supplied by editors may be hosted by external providers.</p><h2>Sessions and abuse prevention</h2><p>Authentication uses browser session storage mechanisms, including cookies and local storage managed by Netlify Identity. These support sign-in and are not used by this application for advertising. No advertising pixels or analytics trackers have been added.</p><p>To reduce automated abuse, the application stores short-lived rate-limit counters keyed to a one-way hash derived from a network address or account identifier. The application does not store raw network addresses in those counters. Netlify may separately process request information as part of hosting and security.</p><h2>Access and removal</h2><p>You can update your display name and password from your reader account, remove saved stories there, and use your private subscription link to unsubscribe. For access, correction, or deletion requests concerning comments, contact messages, or your account, <a href="/contact">contact the O2 Media team</a> using the email associated with the record. The team may need to verify ownership before making changes.</p><h2>Community guidelines</h2><p>Keep comments relevant, constructive, and respectful. Do not post private information, impersonation, harassment, spam, or content you lack permission to share. Editors review comments before publication and may reject or remove comments that do not meet these guidelines.</p></div></section></O2Layout>
